      "t": "As blockchain investing falls out of vogue, a16z Crypto rebrands as a16z Frontier",
      "d": "The digital asset unit, helmed by Chris Dixon, broadens its scope.",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/22/as-blockchain-investing-falls-out-of-vogue-a16z-crypto-rebrands-as-a16z-frontier/",
      "m": "10. 22. PM 10:34",
      "ts": 1792708494000,
      "fullText": "In Brief Posted: 3:34 PM PDT · October 22, 2026 Image Credits: Darrell Etherington/TechCrunch Marina Temkin As blockchain investing falls out of vogue, a16z Crypto rebrands as a16z Frontier In a sign that crypto and blockchain-focused investing has receded in importance, Andreessen Horowitz announced Thursday that it is renaming its digital asset unit from a16z Crypto to a16z Frontier. The practice, helmed by Chris Dixon, has raised nearly $10 billion across five funds since launching in 2018, backing some of the sector&#8217;s biggest wins, including Coinbase. Yet for years, a16z and rival venture firms struggled to push crypto’s utility beyond financial rails, trading applications, and speculative assets. Under the new name, the team is broadening its mandate to focus on emerging technologies, be it AI, robotics, or “new kinds of networks” connecting humans and machines. Yet, the group isn’t abandoning crypto. Dixon wrote in a blog post that blockchain technology could “give new networks native economic capabilities.&#8221; Alongside Dixon, a16z Frontier&#8217;s general partners include Eddy Lazzarin and Guy Wuollet. Meanwhile, Ali Yahya, who joined the crypto strategy as its first investor in 2017, has left the firm, according to The Information . Topics a16z , a16z crypto , In Brief , Venture November 4 Boston Buy One Pass, Get a Second Free Cover more ground at TechCrunch&#8217;s ultimate founder bootcamp of the year by bringing your co-founder or partner for free Book before the BOGO deal expires Register Now Newsletters See More Subscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news TechCrunch Daily News Every weekday and Sunday, you can get the best of TechCrunch’s coverage. TechCrunch Mobility TechCrunch Mobility is your destination for transportation news and insight. Startups Weekly Startups are the core of TechCrunch, so get our best coverage delivered weekly. StrictlyVC Provides movers and shakers with the info they need to start their day. No newsletters selec"
