    {
      "s": "TechCrunch",
      "t": "TechCrunch Disrupt 2026 Startup Battlefield 200: Celebrating outstanding achievements",
      "d": "Among the Startup Battlefield 200 were many industry-defining companies exhibiting and pitching on the Showcase Stage. Here are the standouts.",
      "u": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/22/techcrunch-disrupt-2026-startup-battlefield-200-celebrating-outstanding-achievements/",
      "m": "10. 22. PM 04:00",
      "ts": 1792684800000,
      "fullText": "This year, TechCrunch Disrupt showcased the incredible talent and groundbreaking ideas of our 2026 Startup Battlefield 200 cohort . Out of thousands of applications, we selected 200 of the most promising startups, each bringing unique innovations to their respective industries. The competition culminated in an electrifying event where these startups had the opportunity to pitch and demonstrate their solutions live over three days. From the top 20 finalists , TechCrunch editorial selected the top five companies that then battled it out for the $100,000 equity-free prize and the coveted Disrupt Cup. The well-deserved win went to Intero Biosystems , with a strong runner-up, Apate . Among the Startup Battlefield 200 were many industry-defining companies exhibiting and pitching on the Showcase Stage. Here are the standouts: Best Showcase Stage pitch by industry group Built World Lola Vision Systems provides a full-stack AI platform delivering sensor fusion, secure communications, and real-time inference on today&#8217;s hardware, with purpose-built silicon on the horizon. Sustainability Krokos Bio is growing nature’s most valuable ingredients, in a way that is cheaper and more reliable, starting with saffron. Enterprise Group 1 Rein Security is the security layer for custom-built enterprise agents — the production AI agents running businesses worldwide. Enterprise Group 2 Lumai is the optical compute company addressing scalable AI in the inference era. Health Uhura Bionics has developed a bionic larynx for singing, laughing, and translating emotions. Consumer Maka is delivering developmentally curated shows parents trust and kids love — powered by AI. Best Booth Legali AI is providing a trauma-informed AI legal companion and ecosystem for the middle class and AI-native firms, with a focus on women who&#8217;ve faced abuse. Their all-pink, female-focused booth was a standout on the Expo Floor. Visitors would write empowering messages to women on sticky notes and place the"
